<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42312" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sălernum</span></b> , i,
		n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				maritime town in the Picentine territory</i>, now <i>Salerno</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5,
				9, § 70</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 32,
			29</span></i>; <i><span class="en">34, 45</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Vell.
				1, 15, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 15,
			1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 2, 425</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sălernitānus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>Salernian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">latebra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					13, 3, 5, § 25</span></i>
			 (Jahn, Salurnitanus): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 6, 8, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Să-lernus</span></b> ,
			i, m., <i>an inhabitant of
				Salernum</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pugnax,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					8, 853</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
